USC: give an integer instruction's second destination its own temporaries

On cores with the vector instruction set an integer instruction's results
go to the scalar temporaries USC_TEMPREG_VECTEMPDEST+chan and are then moved
into the vector destination.  Both destinations of a two-destination
instruction (MUL2 and MAD2's high and low words, ADD2's carry) used the
same temporaries, so the second result overwrote the first, and sDest2 was
also read for instructions that have only one destination.  Use
USC_TEMPREG_VECTEMPDEST2 for the second destination and only store it when
the instruction has one.

